💡 **SUGGESTION: token accounting walks the ledger linearly per group member — O(groups × members × entries)**

```dart
final seq = view.seqs.seqOf(id);
if (seq != null) tokens += ledger.entryAtSeq(seq)?.tokens ?? 0;
```

`ContextLedger.entryAtSeq` is a linear scan over all entries (`ledger.dart:66-71`), and this loop runs per member of every expand-carrier group. Same pattern in `_hideAction`'s `freedTokens` loop (`expand_tool.dart:366-369`). Fine at today's session sizes and bounded by `judgePreviewEntries`-scale ledgers, but it's free to fix while here: build a `Map<String, LedgerEntry>` (or `seq → entry`) once per pass next to `byId` and look up directly. Not blocking — just avoid the quadratic trap being copied into the next pass.

