This is a verbatim copy of `StructuredCompactor._refreshState()` (`engine.dart:606-614`), including the non-obvious usage-zeroing convention ("rebuilt messages carry no trustworthy usage"). The PR description itself leans on that contract ("the same contract the engine's own state refresh relies on") — but the contract now lives in two places, and a future tweak to one (e.g., anchoring usage differently after #387-style rebuilds) will silently diverge the tool from the engine.

